  "id": "COMPOUND:26749 - PROTEIN:5837",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 1-Oxo-2H-Isoquinoline-4-Carboxylic Acid and SN12K1 through a series of target interactions involving dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinases. This compound appears to act as a target for multiple compounds, including 6-Acetonyldihydrochelerythrine, Ascidiathiazone B, and CID 21778290, all of which are known to target SN12K1. The shared target relationship indicates that 1-Oxo-2H-Isoquinoline-4-Carboxylic Acid may exert its biological effects through a common mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of these protein kinases. The evidence suggests a possible functional link between the compound and SN12K1, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be elucidated. The consistency across different compounds targeting SN12K1 supports the hypothesis that 1-Oxo-2H-Isoquinoline-4-Carboxylic Acid may influence SN12K1 through a shared pathway, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm this relationship.",
